<title>USA: CBOT clearinghouse buys $100 mln default insurance.</title>
<headline>CBOT clearinghouse buys $100 mln default insurance.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Board of Trade Clearing Corp (BOTCC), the independent clearinghouse of the Chicago Board of Trade, said Tuesday it had contracted to buy a $100 million insurance policy designed for use in the event of a catastrophic member default.</p>
<p>The policy is issued by Lexington Insurance Co, a unit of American International Group Inc.</p>
<p>The clearinghouse also said it earned a AAA rating from Standard &amp; Poor's Corp on April 17.</p>
<p>&quot;By preparing for any eventuality, no matter how unlikely, the BOTCC has weathered every financial crisis of the last 70 years without a single loss caused by clearing member default,&quot; BOTCC President and Chief Executive John Hiatt said in a statement.</p>
<p>Chicago Derivatives Desk ((312-408-8750))</p>
<p>E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com</p>
